title: 'Polkadot: Verify the workers at startup'
doc:
- audience:
  - Node Dev
  - Node Operator
  description: |-
    Closes #8117

    Today, `polkadot` checks that its PVF workers are running the same version at startup, but the
    workers' other security checks (landlock, seccomp, unshare/change-root, clone, etc.) only run
    when a worker is actually spawned. If the node is not yet part of the active validator set, an
    operator running a misconfigured or under-sandboxed worker has no way to find out, until the
    node starts validating, loses rewards, and degrades the network.

    This PR runs those checks at startup too, the same way the version check already does:
    `polkadot` invokes `execute-worker --check-security-features --worker-dir-path <workers-path>`
    once before the node starts, and refuses to start if the worker binary is missing or fails its
    security checks. This way operators are informed immediately, rather than only once the node
    is selected as a validator.
crates:
- name: polkadot-node-core-pvf-common
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-cli
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot
  bump: minor
